# An allowlist. Everything in the build context stays out of the image
# unless named below, so a new file in the working tree (a scratch note, a
# venv, data/, the .nrfutil-bin/ that bin/flash-dongle.sh leaves behind)
# needs no entry here to stay out. push-to-host.sh takes its list from git
# for the same reason; Docker cannot ask git before COPY, so what the
# container runs is listed instead: the package, the vendored sniffer, the
# entrypoint and the requirements the Dockerfile installs first.
# config/ (config.toml, devices.json, credentials.toml, alerts.env, ha.env)
# and data/ are volumes at run time and never part of the image.
*
!requirements.txt
!bin/threadwatch
!threadwatch/
!vendor/
# The deployed commit, which config.repo_commit() reads when there is no
# .git -- and there is none here, deliberately (a build context with the
# whole history in it is not what the image needs). Absent, --version,
# status and doctor report no commit for the image; see the REVISION build
# argument in the Dockerfile and docs/DOCKER.md.
!REVISION
# Caches inside the trees allowed above.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
